{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEPW6J1GY9Y9cNWvsf5b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it in `bot.py`: a `save_fact` should now only re-cache the new fact (about 15 tokens) instead of the whole ~1050-token prompt. I checked this with an offline simulation, not against the real API.\n\n**What was wrong:** the instructions and the athlete's data were sent as one cached block. Saving a fact changed that block, so the next call found nothing cached (`cache_read_input_tokens: 0` in the log) and paid to write everything again, instructions included.\n\n**Why the obvious fix wouldn't have worked:** the usual answer is a second cache marker right after the instructions, as `notes/two-cache-control-segments...` suggests. But Sonnet 4.5 only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens. With the default tools, the tools plus instructions come to about 940 tokens (estimated from your log), so the API would silently skip that marker on most messages. The simulation shows that version still re-writing ~1060 tokens after a save.\n\n**What I changed** (`athlete_context` / `build_system` in `bot.py`):\n- The instructions are their own block, identical for every user and day, with their own marker.\n- The athlete data follows, from most to least stable: profile and language, then the date and the facts header, then one block per fact. The marker is on the last block.\n- `save_fact` only ever adds a fact at the end, so after a save the previous prompt is still an exact prefix of the new one. The API checks up to about 20 blocks back from a marker, so the new call reads the old prompt from cache and writes only the new fact.\n- I removed the `(none yet)` placeholder so the first fact adds a block instead of replacing one.\n- Tools and the keyword filtering are unchanged, as `NOTES.md` asks. The request uses 2 of the 4 allowed markers.\n\n**How I checked it:** `python3 -I tests/test_prompt_cache.py` simulates the cache with the 1024-token minimum and the 20-block look-back. Token counts are estimated from character counts, fitted to your log.\n\n| After a `save_fact` | Read from cache | Written to cache |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before | 0 | ~1060 |\n| Instructions marker only | 0 | ~1060 |\n| Now | ~1047 | ~14 |\n\nOn the live bot, the round right after a `save_fact` should show `cache_read_input_tokens` close to the previous value and `cache_creation_input_tokens` around 15–30.\n\n**Things that still force a full re-cache:**\n- **Editing facts:** changing or deleting a saved fact, or sending only some facts per message, breaks the \"only add at the end\" rule.\n- **Tool groups:** a message that pulls in the plan or race tools re-caches everything once. That was true before and is the price of keeping the filtering.\n- **New athletes:** an athlete with no facts yet is around 1000 tokens and may not be cached at all, as before. That goes away after a fact or two.\n\n`ANSWER.md` has the full write-up, and I updated the caching line in `README.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2031,"cache_read_input_tokens":41958,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2031},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bcbb9cf-f1de-4b82-8a9e-f820749877cb","uuid":"ceb2cbe4-1d25-46bb-a67a-cd795af46b68","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:52:51.197Z","request_id":"req_011CgEPW62PLuH4yuiCP78no"}
